Built on Wine
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything Cellar does happens inside Wine, the Windows compatibility layer
that reimplements the Win32 API on macOS. Cellar is a launcher over it — a
runner catalogue, bottles, profiles and a front-end. The Win32 implementation
is Wine's.

  Wine      Copyright (C) 1993-2026 the Wine project authors
            LGPL-2.1-or-later — https://www.winehq.org/
            Source: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine

Cellar does not bundle Wine in its source or release artifacts; it downloads
prebuilt LGPL Wine runners at run time (see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md), and it
carries no modifications to Wine. With thanks also to:

  CodeWeavers  — the public LGPL macOS patches (Mac driver, msync) in the runners
                 https://github.com/CodeWeavers/wine
  WineForge    — the default runner build      https://github.com/Alien4042x/WineForge
  Sikarugir    — the Wine 10 runner + template https://github.com/Sikarugir-App
  Gcenx        — the Game Porting Toolkit build https://github.com/Gcenx
  SteamRE      — DepotDownloader (GPL-2.0)      https://github.com/SteamRE/DepotDownloader

